    "summary": "Rain‑soaked Red Rocks ’82 delivers a monster set with Crazy Fingers & The Other One",
    "review": "July 29, 1982 at Red Rocks was a rain‑drenched night that turned into one of the summer’s most electric shows. The first set started slow and spacey under a steady drizzle, but by the time the band hit “Cold Rain And Snow” they were locked in, launching a blistering segue into “Samson & Delilah” and then ripping through a rare, soaring “Crazy Fingers.” Jerry’s leads cut cleanly through the mist, Phil’s bass rumbled like thunder, and Brent’s keyboards added that trippy undercurrent that kept the jam flowing. The second set built an unstoppable arc: a fierce “I Need A Miracle” jam that swelled into a stormy “The Other One,” followed by a rollicking run through “Goin’ Down The Road Feeling Bad,” “Wharf Rat,” and a joyous “Good Lovin’.”\n\nFor anyone wanting to relive this night, the front‑of‑board audience tape (gd82-07-29.fob-senn421.wise.4981.sbeok.shnf) is the stand‑out source – it captures the rain‑soaked ambience, deep bass, and crisp guitar while staying clean enough for a full‑show listen. Whether you’re chasing Jerry’s shredding on “Crazy Fingers,” Phil’s “bass bombs” on The Other One, or just want to soak up that high‑energy Red Rocks vibe, this recording gives you the best window into what made July ’82 such a monster night.",
